==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|finicking}}, from {{m|en|finical}}, from {{m|en|fine}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# {{label|en|informal}} [[fastidious|Fastidious]] and [[fussy]]; difficult to [[please]]; [[exacting]], especially about [[detail]]s.
#: ''The baby was '''finicky''' until her diaper was changed.
# {{label|en|informal}} Demanding, requiring above-normal care.
#: ''The lawnmower is a bit '''finicky''' in cold weather.''

====Usage notes====
* The forms {{m|en|finickier}} and {{m|en|finickiest}} also exist, but are quite rare, and perhaps nonstandard. The forms {{m|en||more finicky}} and {{m|en||most finicky}} are much more common, and certainly standard.

====Synonyms====
* [[fastidious]], [[fussy]]
* See [[wikisaurus:fastidious]]

====Derived terms====
* [[finickiness]]
* [[finickity]]

